
HISTORY of GRAF-D.PPE
=========================================================================

v2.00  05/07/93    * Initial release of the rewrite.  GRAF-D used to be
                     known as ANSI-D before RIPscrip came along.  It
                     would not be fair to RIP if I kept the name the
                     same.  :-)
                   
v2.10  05/27/93    * Added a new parameter for the PPE -- /AUTO.  If you 
                     want to force your users to make user of ANSI or 
                     RIPscript (if detected) then you'll want to use 
                     this switch.
                   
                   * Reworked the way that the PPE makes you aware that 
                     you have configured your system improperly.  More 
                     precisely, if you have told PCBoard to default to 
                     graphics mode it will cause GRAF-D to malfunction.
                     
                     In previous versions, the PPE would attempt to 
                     leave a message to the SysOp.  However, a lot of 
                     the SysOps were getting "No room for text" 
                     messages.  Now a simple box is printed to the 
                     screen (not the modem).  This should make it better 
                     for all.

v2.11  05/27/93    * Looks like I optimized the code just a *bit* <no pun
                     intended> too much.  :-)  If you pressed enter when
                     ANSI is detected it would set you to non-graphics
                     mode.  Fixed.
                     
v2.20  09/10/93    * Added a new parameter -- /NORIP.  If you want GRAF-D
                     to skip sending the RIPscrip auto-detection sequence,
                     use this parameter.  Because the sequence is not sent,
                     RIP capabilities will not be automatically sensed by
                     GRAF-D.
                     
                   * Added a new parameter -- /NOQUICK.  This parameter
                     will disable the user's ability to skip the welcome
                     screen using the "Q" subcommand.
                     
                   * Added the /DEBUG and /DELAY command line parameters.
                     Refer to GRAF-D.DOC for additional details.
                     
v2.30  08/31/94    * Stripped out the graphics detection routines because
                     they are no longer necessary.  With v15.2, PCBoard now
                     detects ANSI and RIP just after the connection is made.
                     Therefore, the CHECKRIP() and ANSION() functions can be
                     used to save an awful lot of code.

                   * Removed the FIELDLEN parameter from the INPUTSTR
                     statement.  It really never served a useful purpose
                     because it requires ANSI to be detected.  In the past,
                     it was not a problem and would be ignored. However,
                     with v15.2 of PCBoard checking for ANSI and RIPscrip at
                     login, it would put parentheses around the answer field
                     thereby breaking some scripts.

                   * Removed the /WAIT, /DELAY, and /DEBUG command line
                     parameters since all detection is done by PCBoard now.

                   * Renamed the history file from HISTORY.TXT to GRAF-D.HIS.
                     Then again, you knew that already if you're reading this.
                     <grin>

v2.31  11/07/94    * Okay, I got a little axe-happy.  In my efforts to gut
                     my own detection routines and replace them with PPL's,
                     I removed the ESC = CHR(27) line.  This would cause
                     problems for anyone using the /COMPATIBLE mode because
                     the ANSI escape coudes would not be sent out properly.
                     Fixed.
